.TH tutail n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tutail
.PP
Tail\-like helpers.
.CS
package require tclutils::tutail
puts [::tclutils::tutail::file logfile.txt 50]
.CE
.PP
Commands:
.IP \(bu
\fBtext text ?count?\fR \-\- the last \fBcount\fR lines (default 10)
.IP \(bu
\fBfile path ?count? ?\-encoding enc?\fR \-\- the same for a file (default utf\-8)
.PP
As with \fBtail \-n\fR, the result keeps the line ends: every line ends with \fB\en\fR, except the last line of the input when it has none. \fBtext\fR and \fBfile\fR give the same result (0.2; 0.1 \fBtext\fR took the empty rest after a final \fB\en\fR as a line, \fBfile\fR dropped every line end). A count that is not an integer >= 0 raises \fBTCLUTILS TUTAIL COUNT\fR. Print with \fBputs \-nonewline\fR.
